{"id": "EUVD-2015-9429", "enisaUuid": "b7bf42b3-cb44-3467-bf3f-4fe664b54832", "description": "Aspose Doc Exporter plugin for WordPress before 2.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to download arbitrary files by passing unsanitized paths to readfile(). Attackers can send GET requests to aspose_doc_exporter_download.php with the 'file' parameter set to values like ../../../wp-config.php to retrieve database credentials. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-23.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:31:24", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/36559", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/131167/", "https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/043aa583-a81d-4565-bf65-83252b8f1f96", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/aspose-words-file-download.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/aspose-doc-exporter/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/aspose-doc-exporter-wordpress-plugin-2.0-path-traversal-via-aspose-doc-exporter-download-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2015-20123", "GHSA-fv35-wmpq-m6x4"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b5f92f13-a999-35bb-94af-ecbe0ab65c8d", "product": {"name": "Aspose Doc Exporter", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}, "product_version": "1.0 <2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6b064ab5-6a9f-3e40-a4f4-af3a90dc72a7", "vendor": {"name": "Aspose"}}], "isExploited": false}